 For LIBERO, we train on a single node with 8 GPUs. For RoboTwin, we use 64 GPUs to accelerate training. You can try reducing the GPU count or training epochs.
 
+### 3) Wan LoRA with full ActionDiT training
+
+Select `model=fastwam_lora` to freeze the pretrained Wan video backbone and train
+LoRA in its transformer attention projections (`q/k/v/o` for self and cross
+attention) and both feed-forward projections. The default rank and alpha are
+16, with zero dropout. The entire action expert and optional proprio encoder
+remain trainable; VAE and text encoder stay frozen. This adds no dependencies.
+
+```bash
+# Use the prepared training environment and local pretrained weights.
+source ../migration/training_envs/activate.sh fastwam
+bash scripts/train_zero1.sh 1 \
+  task=libero_uncond_2cam224_1e-4 model=fastwam_lora \
+  model.video_lora.rank=16 model.video_lora.alpha=16
+```
+
+Prepare the dataset, statistics and T5 embedding cache as above before launching.
+The preset uses official native Wan weights (`redirect_common_files=false`) and
+the ActionDiT initializer at `$FASTWAM_ACTION_DIT_PATH` (falling back to
+`checkpoints/ActionDiT_linear_interp_Wan22_alphascale_1024hdim.pt`). GPU count and
+batch size should be chosen for the available hardware.
+
+Weight checkpoints contain only the Wan adapters, the **complete** action expert,
+the optional proprio encoder and LoRA settings. Reload them with the same Wan
+base and matching LoRA settings using `resume=/path/to/weights.pt` (weights only).
+Dense FastWAM checkpoints require the original `model=fastwam` preset, since
+compact adapters depend on an unchanged pretrained Wan base.
+Use `resume=/path/to/state_directory` for the existing Accelerate
+resume path, including optimizer/scheduler progress, and keep the same model
+settings. Those full training-state snapshots still include the frozen backbone.
+Selecting the original `model=fastwam` retains full training of both experts.
+
+### 4) Action expert only
+
+Use `model=fastwam_action_only` to freeze Wan completely and train the full
+ActionDiT plus the small proprio projection. Wan runs under `no_grad`; only the
+clean first video frame is encoded and used to prepare per-layer video K/V.
+The action branch attends those frozen features and optimizes action loss only.
+This preserves the standard FastWAM first-frame attention layout and requires
+`first_frame_causal` or `per_frame_causal` video attention. Video LoRA and
+`compile_training_denoise` are disabled in this mode.
+
+```bash
+source ../migration/training_envs/activate.sh fastwam
+bash scripts/train_zero1.sh 1 \
+  task=libero_uncond_2cam224_1e-4 model=fastwam_action_only
+```
+
+Keep the dataset's action horizon and sampling configuration; the training path
+selects the initial video frame internally. Dataset decoding may still read the
+configured clip on CPU. Weight exports and full-state snapshots include the
+frozen Wan base, so dense weight warm starts remain self-contained. Resume full
+training state with the same Action-only preset; a `.pt` resume restores weights
+only. Dataset/statistics/T5-cache preparation is unchanged.
+
